Carafe: the profiler counts each sampled thread's time by the calls nearest the thread's start, so the stages of a
game's frame loop show without knowing the game. While the thread is paused it follows the x86 frame chain from the
guest's EBP to the thread's start, up to 64 frames; a chain that breaks before it is left out. The return addresses
one to six calls from the start each count the sample, and every report adds a stages line with the three busiest
at each level, as shares of the samples that reached the start.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

